2026-11-13: the one-time ClickUp reorganization is done; the exception has ended

Record, not a new ruling. Under Coach Ed's ruling of 2026-11-13 ("yes, approved. the manager can carry it out", then "Yes, apply all" to the archive, status and new-task lists) the manager:

created folders 1 MVP Launch, 2 Owner, 3 After Launch, 5 Archive and their lists; renamed the FAS folder "4 Financial Accounting System" and Online Shop MVP "Online Shop (Q1 2027)";
moved all 149 tasks of the old Sante Site MVP list (26 top-level tasks with their subtasks); no task was deleted;
archived 16 legacy Billing tasks in place (Phases 6 finished parts, 7, 8, 9 and P11.0), each parent with a comment naming the B task that replaces it;
corrected 8 stale statuses, each with an evidence comment; ACCEPTED and Completed were not set;
created 14 missing tasks (ids z8uq9mek5p to z8uq9mek63) from the 2026-11-13 code check;
created the tag waiting-on-coach-ed and put it on 13 tasks; set 5 dependencies.

From here the standing rule applies again: the manager creates no ClickUp task and writes only on this log. Coordinators own the status of their tasks. Each new task needs its own approved plan before any build; none is approved by being created.

Left for Coach Ed in the ClickUp app (the API cannot do it): drag Admin, Compliance Calendar and Social Media into "2 Owner" and Online Shop (Q1 2027) into "3 After Launch"; delete the empty Sante Site MVP list.
